            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter embolization of a coronary artery fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>281-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A coronary artery fistula from left anterior descending coronary artery to right ventricle was successfully occluded by transcatheter embolization using steel coils. Transcatheter embolization seems to be the treatment of choice for coronary artery fistulas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
